1. **Graph-toggle state changes unobserved.** t=0110 (Sign Up) shows "Disable Graph View (User Study Persona 1)" **UNCHECKED**. The first later view of the same setting, t=0400 (Profile), shows it **CHECKED**. No sampled frame captures the change.
2. **No "Graph View" control exists anywhere.** Across every planner frame (t=0130–0650) the toolbar is exactly: `Hide Sidebar | Show/Hide Recs … Help | Open/Close Dashboard | Profile | Sign Out`. No Graph View / node-link entry point is present, and no `graph` surface occurs in this range. Consistent with the brief's "Vergleichsgruppe (Ohne Graph)".
3. **Program/level self-contradiction at t=0130–0140.** The open Setup modal reads "Bachelor Informatics (033 521)" while the surface behind it simultaneously shows English **master** categories and the banner "No **master** courses are planned yet. / Do you want to fill the table with the prebuilt **master** plan?". At t=0150 (modal closed) the same banner reads "No **bachelor** courses are planned yet … prebuilt **bachelor** plan?" and the sidebar has swapped to German bachelor categories.
